<!--
    A jump-table guard whose tested value has no set bit below bit 31 aborted
    the decompile.

    widemask (source: tests/stages/src/nzmask_wide_stride.s) tests bit 61 of a
    word, Swift's small-string flag, before an indirect tail jump through a
    relative pointer. Recovering that jump as a switch pulls the guard
    (x21 & 0x2000000000000000) == 0 back through the value's non-zero mask, and
    CircleRange::set_nz_mask used the mask's lowest set bit, 61, as the shift of
    its int4 stride: 1 << 61 overflows (a panic with overflow checks, a garbage
    or negative stride without them; C++ rangeutil.cc setNZMask has the same
    int4 shift). The stride is now capped at 1 << 30, which still holds every
    value the mask allows.

    Stage: S2 flow classification (jump-table guard ranges). No option: a strict
    fix. Single pass, since an abort discards every assertion: the function now
    decompiles to the full body with both tail jumps.

    Build: clang -target aarch64-linux-gnu -c nzmask_wide_stride.s; the .text
    bytes are the chunk below.
-->
